YES, it certainly did!  The results are very spectacular!  For Mapped
RT-11 Monitors, the two choices are the SDHX.SYS and SDSX.SYS
which have already been described.  By combining SDHX.SYS and
DBGSYM.SAV, all of the symbolic debugging is available.

HOWEVER, as I have mentioned, SDHX.SYS (renamed as SDX.SYS
to work under RT-11) freezes EVERYTHING including interrupts for the
clock.

On the other hand, I just attempted to check out VDT by starting it as
a foreground job and obtaining the contents of 14,16 (vector for BPT).
As per the suggestion for using ODT with device handlers, it is then
possible under certain conditions (ask if you are interested) to restore
the BPT vector values and execute a background program under VDT
breakpoint control WITHOUT all those great features in SDHX.SYS,
BUT with all other jobs and the rest of the RT-11 operating system
remaining UNFROZEN!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!   So IT  IS  POSSIBLE!!!!!
AND the best aspect of starting VDT as a foreground job is that it
does not need to first be LINKed into the SAV file.

BUT  DEC never did combine those two aspects.  The question is
if anyone else is actually writing and debugging any programs to be
run under RT-11.  Even if someone is just interested, I don't know
if the effort of enhancing VDT is worth while just for myself.  Does
anyone else still write and debug programs using SDX.SYS, ODT
or VDT under RT-11?  If I have 50 more years of writing RT-11
programs, well maybe for myself.  But with perhaps 10 years, .....

Jerome Fine

