No idea. I don't have any sources. The Symbolic Debugger is a DEC 
product, and only comes in binary form. Also, it understands both 
MACRO-11, FORTRAN 77 and COBOL-81. In addition, it can perform all kind 
of advanced things conditionally at breakpoints or tracepoints, as well 
as managing breaks and traces in different overlays. (Even when those 
overlays are not in memory when you give the commands.) It uses a couple 
of hundred words of address space in your program, and the rest is 
outside. It's not a device, and it does not freeze anything else 
running. In fact, any user can run the symbolic debugger concurrently 
with other users without interference.

Does that sound like DBG.MAC?

(I do wish I could find the sources for all kind of layered products, 
but I have not had any luck so far.)

	Johnny



