Thanks. No, I had not read that manual before. But now, having done so, 
I dare say that there are no relationship between DBG-11 and the 
symbolic debugger product I'm talking about.

> In addition, Under RT-11, there is a separate program,
> DBGSYM.SAV, which is used to read the FOOBAR.STB
> file and set up the symbolic names.  If I understand the
> RSX-11 interface, the ";A" command initiates that operation.

Uh... No... (Where did you get that???)

First of all, the symbolic debugger automatically reads in the whole 
.STB file when you start running the program. No action at all is 
required on your part. Your symbols are just there, when you start your 
session. (Yes, the symbolic debugger figures out the correct STB file 
that matches your task file.) Second, in addition to global symbols, the 
symbolic debugger also handles local symbols. To manage this, a symbol 
is actually a path, as you might have several identical symbols in 
different modules. So a symbol is actually all the module names and the 
symbol name as a long string, with each component separated by a backslash.
And symbols can be expressed in relative or absolute form.

Finally, if you want to specify by hand which .STB file to use, the 
command is "SET STB filename"

If you want to define symbols of your own, the command is "DEFINE symbol 
= value".

> All in all, the file DBG.MAC probably has both RSX-11 and
> RT-11 specific code, parts of which are completely omitted
> depending on which operating system is the target.  DEC
> often seems to do this sort of thing.
>
> Can you confirm any of this?

I would say there seems to be no similarities between DBG-11 and the 
symbolic debugger. DBG-11 have about the same capabilities and syntax as 
ODT under RSX, with the exception that ODT does not handle symbolic 
names. XDT (the kernel debugger for RSX) comes even closer, as the 
syntax is very much the same, and XDT also can handle some symbolic 
address names in the kernel.

The capabilities of the symbolic debugger far surpass all of this. I 
suspect it is not possible to get that capability under RT-11. Oh well.

